module Core

### Represents the aggregate protocol for plain value records.
### `RecordType` identifies the value-semantics category: copying duplicates the value and the
### layout is structural. It does NOT imply `Equatable`/`Hashable` — equality and hashing are
### capabilities a record opts into explicitly (`obeys Equatable`/`Hashable` + a hand-written
### `eq`/`hash`, enforced by RF-S702), never an automatic consequence of being a record. Bundling
### them here promised conformance with no body behind it (a record that never declares `eq` would
### still "obey" Equatable), which let constrained generics like `List[T].eq` instantiate for a
### non-equatable element and emit a call to the abstract `Equatable.eq` → linker error.
protocol RecordType obeys Diagnosable, Serializable
  pass
